completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible: 4.3-stable, 4.4-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Fedora 31 (KDE Plasma) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon(TM) HD8800 Series (PITCAIRN, DRM 3.38.0, 5.8.18-100.fc31.x86_64, LLVM 9.0.1) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-4770 CPU @ 3.40GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nGodot throws a lot of errors when you select a node with attached script loaded from resource pack:\n\n```\n  ERROR: Attempt to open script 'res://root.gd' resulted in error 'File not found'.\n  ERROR: Failed loading resource: res://root.gd. Make sure resources have been imported by opening the project in the editor at least once.\n```\n\nHowever, everything works fine and “unfound” script runs as expected.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open library project.\n2. Export project as resource pack to consumer project.\n3. Open consumer project.\n4. Load resource pack and instantiate scene.\n5. Start scene.\n6. Select node with attached script (in MRP it's `root`) in remote inspector tree.\n7. See errors in console.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nConsumer project already have `library.pck`. So you can skip 1 and 2 steps for reproduce. \n\n[library-base.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19503506/library-base.zip)\n\n[library-consumer.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19503508/library-consumer.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gith